{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The sweeper (normally fired by its 5-minute timer) - the whole 'save' step made mechanical. For EVERY registered repo with an origin it runs fetch --prune, so repo_state's and the git sensor's ahead/behind numbers are real without a click. For repos flagged autocommit it stages and commits when the tree is dirty, then pushes whenever the branch tracks a remote and holds anything unpushed (an unpublished branch is reported, not published). NEVER commits on master/main: 'branches always' is enforced here (result refused_default_branch), which is what makes flagging canon and the overlay safe. A clean tree, a git-less box, or an absent registry is a free no-op. Returns {swept, committed, pushed, fetched, results:[{repo, fetched, branch, result, paths, push, ...}]}.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"xlqhrg1a02521633dv7","readers":[],"time":1788639906762,"username":"system","writers":[]}